<%# THE PAGE'S OWN HEADING, plus the one control that spends money.

    THE QUERY IS PRINTED, not merely implied by the person's name. It is assembled
    from the person plus their team (Appearances::GatherReferencePhotos#query), so it
    is not what the operator would have typed — and he cannot judge a search whose
    question he cannot see. %>
<header class="space-y-3">
  <div>
    <p class="label-upper text-muted">Photo scouting</p>
    <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-heading leading-tight">
      <%= @person.full_name %>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">
      <%= link_to "back to #{@person.full_name}", person_path(@person.slug),
            class: "hover:text-primary underline" %>
      <% if @appearance %>
        &middot;
        <%= link_to "the look this files against", person_appearance_path(@person.slug, @appearance.slug),
              class: "hover:text-primary underline" %>
      <% end %>
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="text-sm text-body max-w-2xl">
    What the search found, what the ranking picked, and
    <strong class="text-heading">what you would have picked instead</strong>.
    Judge the search as well as the pick: every candidate it returned is below, in the
    order it returned them.
  </p>

  <% if @appearance %>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-subtle bg-surface-alt p-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <% if @search_available %>
          <p class="text-xs text-heading font-bold">
            Searching with <span class="font-mono"><%= @search_provider %></span>
          </p>
          <p class="text-2xs text-muted break-words">
            Query: &ldquo;<%= @search_query %>&rdquo;
          </p>
        <% else %>
          <p data-test="search-unconfigured" class="text-xs text-heading font-bold">
            No provider is configured
          </p>
          <p class="text-2xs text-muted break-words">
            Nothing can be searched. Set
            <span class="font-mono text-warning-ink"><%= Appearances::ImageSearch::Serper::API_KEY_ENV %></span>
            for a paid provider; the keyless one should have covered this, so its
            absence here means the registry was changed.
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%# ADMINS ONLY, matching the controller. A search buys one provider query plus
          up to VISION_SHORTLIST vision classifications, and hub signup is open — so a
          button shown to everyone is a purchase offered to everyone. A control nobody
          but an admin may use is furniture on every other reader's page. %>
      <% if admin? && @search_available %>
        <%= button_to "Search the web", search_person_scouting_path(@person.slug),
              method: :post, class: "btn btn-sm btn-primary shrink-0",
              form: { data: { test: "scouting-search-button" } } %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</header>
